.TH MARKCHECK 1 "2026-08-14" "markcheck 2.4.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
markcheck \- scan text for hidden and invisible Unicode characters
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B markcheck
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects zero\-width characters, bidirectional controls, variation selectors, nonstandard whitespace, invisible format code points, and the Unicode Tags block: code points that render as nothing, or as an ordinary\-looking space, yet occupy distinct bytes. With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
markcheck inspects the byte stream, so it finds marks that ARE bytes. It does not detect statistical (token\-distribution) watermarks, and it does not read C2PA provenance metadata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fR
show this help message and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-strip\fR
write a cleaned copy (FILE.clean.EXT) with hits removed
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
with \-\-strip, overwrite the original (writes a .bak backup unless \-\-no\-backup)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
with \-\-in\-place, skip the .bak backup
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
with \-\-strip on stdin, write cleaned text to stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
emit JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
with \-\-strip, overwrite an existing FILE.clean.EXT
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR CATS
comma\-separated categories to scan (e.g. zero\-width,bidi)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR CATS
comma\-separated categories to skip
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-severity\fR LEVEL
report only hits at or above LEVEL (info, low, medium, high; default info). Narrows scope: \-\-strip and the exit code follow it
.TP
\fB\-\-suspicious\-only\fR
shorthand for \-\-min\-severity medium: drop the annotated, likely\-legitimate hits
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-default\-ignorables\fR
also scan every remaining Unicode default\-ignorable code point (noisy; for forensic use)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR N
refuse inputs larger than N bytes (default 104857600; 0 = unlimited)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-hits\fR N
cap stored hit records at N to bound memory (default 200000; 0 = unlimited)
.TP
\fB\-\-show\fR N
max locations to list (default 20)
.TP
\fB\-\-list\-categories\fR
print the taxonomy and exit
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
no hidden characters were found
.TP
.B 1
hidden characters were found
.TP
.B 2
usage error, or a read or write failed
.TP
.B 130
interrupted
.TP
.B 141
terminated by SIGPIPE (POSIX)
.SH CATEGORIES
.TP
\fBzero\-width\fR
Zero\-advance invisibles (ZWSP, ZWJ, ZWNJ, word joiner, invisible math operators, BOM). ZWJ is also a valid emoji and Indic joiner; likely\-legitimate uses are annotated.
.TP
\fBinvisible\-format\fR
Format and filler code points that render blank (soft hyphen, grapheme joiner, script fillers, interlinear annotation, deprecated format controls).
.TP
\fBbidi\fR
Bidirectional controls. Valid in RTL scripts; the override and isolate members enable Trojan\-Source reordering.
.TP
\fBvariation\-selector\fR
Variation selectors. Normally style glyphs; can carry hidden payloads.
.TP
\fBtag\fR
Unicode Tags block. Invisible; used for text smuggling and prompt injection. Rare in ordinary prose.
.TP
\fBwhitespace\fR
Nonstandard whitespace (NBSP, narrow no\-break space, en and em spaces, line and paragraph separators). Renders like a space but differs from ASCII space; the class behind the 2025 NNBSP fingerprint reports. Common in typeset and word\-processor text; \-\-exclude whitespace to skip.
.TP
\fBdefault\-ignorable\fR
OPT\-IN. Every remaining Unicode Default_Ignorable_Code_Point not covered above, including reserved ranges. Off by default because it is noisy; enable with \-\-include\-default\-ignorables for forensic work.
.SH SEVERITY
Each hit is rated info, low, medium, high. Annotated, likely\-legitimate hits are info. Use \-\-min\-severity or \-\-suspicious\-only to narrow scope; the exit code and \-\-strip follow the same scope.
.SH SEE ALSO
c2patool(1), exiftool(1)
.SH AUTHOR
MavProDev.
